index 40827a86634d0b9c3fbd850b9c28e2cb86e4bef4..2e6129b5c70b957fed1dd7ce26f5372892d6e02c 100644
--- a/docs/editor-setup.md
+++ b/docs/editor-setup.md
@@ -239,3 +239,29 @@ registration information; client buffer forwarding is a separate integration.
 PSR-4 source directories explicitly mapped inside a nested Composer project
 remain dependencies of the consuming application. Their unsaved PHP provider
 changes refresh its registration decisions without merging sibling projects.
+
+### Registered JSON buffer routing
+
+`experimental.phpWorkbenchRegisteredJsonTranslations` advertises standard LSP
+buffer routing for statically registered JSON translation directories. Require
+this capability as well as `phpWorkbenchJsonTranslationResource` before sharing
+custom-root JSON contents. Query admission with the consuming PHP document or
+Composer manifest first, including after a server restart or provider change.
+A successful query records that graph as the navigation context for a closed
+resource, using the same ordered ownership mechanism as returned definitions.
+An open document retains its selected graph until close. Registered consumers
+receive JSON data through normal didOpen/didChange/didClose notifications; the
+workspace JSON discovery filter is unchanged. A unique registered application
+also provides the context for a closed package catalog. Forwarded JSON is never
+parsed as PHP, including while a provider registration is being retired.
+
+Native PHP diagnostics also retain JSON as data. Recovery acknowledges the
+current resource revision without building a PHP AST; PHP fast and slow
+diagnostic collectors leave resource diagnostics to their own language service.
+PHP documents continue through both phases normally.
+
+Composer/project graph reloads replay registered JSON after provider discovery,
+then remap the selected graph and every consuming document revision. Dirty and
+never-saved catalogs therefore survive a graph rebuild and accept following
+changes without a client close/reopen cycle. A selected graph is retained while
+its registration remains valid.
